 "note": "Approximate built-up extent of Philadelphia and its liberties in 1776, traced by hand from William Faden's 'A plan of the city and environs of Philadelphia' (1777, public domain; Library of Congress). The town filled the blocks between the Delaware and about Seventh/Eighth Street, from Vine Street south to Cedar (South) Street, with Southwark below and the Northern Liberties above along the river. The outline is approximate to a few blocks and is labelled so on the map; it is not a survey.",
